[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114794,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The odontogenic sarcomas (OSs) are a group of malignant mixed odontogenic neoplasms in which only the ectomesenchymal component shows microscopic features of malignancy.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114795,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9330/3 Odontogenic sarcomas</p>\r\n<p>9330/3 Ameloblastic fibrosarcoma</p>\r\n<p>9330/3 Ameloblastic fibrodentinosarcoma</p>\r\n<p>9330/3 Ameloblastic fibro-odontosarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114796,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B5J &amp; XH0XD5 Malignant miscellaneous tumours of bone or articular cartilage of other or unspecified sites &amp; Ameloblastic fibrosarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114797,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114798,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ameloblastic fibrosarcoma; ameloblastic fibrodentinosarcoma; ameloblastic fibro-odontosarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114799,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Approximately 75&ndash;80% arise in the mandible with a predilection for the posterior region {28492759; 32508466}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114800,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "<p>Patients present with locally aggressive expansile lesions, with or without pain. Many OSs arise from malignant transformation of a benign precursor.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Early lesions may appear benign radiographically, features reflecting a benign precursor. However, with time, the lesions typically develop poorly defined margins with cortical destruction. Most lesions are unilocular or multilocular radiolucencies, but are occasionally mixed radiolucent/radiopaque {19150219; 28776760}. Tooth displacement, impaction, and root resorption are also possible {28776760}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:34:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114801,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Only about 100&nbsp;cases have been reported {28776760; 32508466}. The M:F&nbsp;ratio is about 1.5:1. The average age at diagnosis is in the third decade of life {25921823; 28776760}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114802,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown; however, more than half of all OSs arise from malignant transformation of a pre-existing benign neoplasm, such as ameloblastic fibroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114803,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>OSs have <em>BRAF</em> p.V600E activating mutations {31899815} in the mesenchymal component {32966885}. Single cases have shown <em>NRAS</em> p.Q61K mutation (mutually exclusive with <em>BRAF</em> p.V600E mutation), <em>EGFR</em> exon&nbsp;20 insertions, <em>MDM2</em> amplification, or aneuploidy {7614208; 31899815; 33867182}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114804,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not reported</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114805,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>OSs contain an epithelial component and an ectomesenchymal component. The epithelial component is cytologically bland and benign. It varies considerably in quantity and morphology, ranging from thin dental lamina&ndash;like strands to larger islands of odontogenic epithelium, with peripheral cells showing nuclear palisading and reverse polarity but not stellate reticulum. The malignant ectomesenchymal component is characterized by hypercellularity, varying degrees of cytological atypia, and increased mitotic activity {21074695; 28492759}. In approximately 10% of cases, dysplastic dentine with or without enamel matrix is produced (ameloblastic fibrodentinosarcoma or ameloblastic fibro-odontosarcoma).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114806,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114807,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The mutations identified (see <em>Pathogenesis</em>, above) are not yet clinically relevant.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114808,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> origin in a tooth-bearing segment of the jaws; a mixed odontogenic neoplasm; a cytologically bland epithelial component; a cytologically malignant ectomesenchymal component.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> evidence of a benign precursor.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114809,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "<p >Although there is no defined eighth-edition Union for International Cancer Control (UICC)&nbsp;/ American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) TNM staging system staging guidance, the use of International Collaboration on Cancer Reporting (ICCR) minimum data set reporting is encouraged {30500289}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:34:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114810,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 150,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases are treated by surgical resection, with an overall recurrence rate of 35% and a disease-related mortality rate of 21% {28776760}. Metastases are usually distant but affect &lt;&nbsp;5% of cases {32508466}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T11:47:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]